Program Bug_2_62_Sqrt_MissingZpScratch;
// Bug 2.62: Methods6502::Sqrt (methods6502.cpp ~3838-3841) and
// Methods6502::InitSqrt16 (methods6502.cpp ~5350-5353) both start with
//   if (as->m_internalZP.count()<4) return;
// with no ErrorHandler::e.Error(...) call on that path - unlike most other
// guarded builtins in this file, which raise a real compiler error in the
// equivalent situation.
//
// CORRECTION to the original KNOWN_BUGS.md writeup, found while writing
// this snippet (re-verified against the live repo per CLAUDE.md's own
// "never trust a snapshot" rule): that `count()<4` guard is actually dead
// code and can never fire. Assembler::m_internalZP is built once, in
// Compiler6502's setup, as
//   RegisterStack(QStringList() << getString("zeropage_internal1") << ... << getString("zeropage_internal4"))
// - four QStringList::operator<< calls happen unconditionally, so the
// resulting list always has exactly 4 entries (some possibly empty
// strings) regardless of whether the project file defines those keys at
// all. RegisterStack::count() just returns m_free.count() as constructed;
// the only method that actually removes an entry (the no-arg Get(), as
// opposed to the index/peek overload) is never called anywhere in live
// (non-commented-out) code, so the free-list size can't shrink at
// runtime either. Confirmed empirically: compiling a Sqrt call with the
// project's zeropage_internal1-4 keys entirely removed does NOT silently
// no-op - it proceeds into InitSqrt16 with empty-string zero page
// addresses and fails at the assembly stage with a real, if confusing,
// error ("Opcode type not implemented or illegal: sty type 0", from an
// `sty <empty>` instruction). This is a real bug with a real, wrong
// documented symptom for the "silent no-op" case: a hard, correctly-
// triggered compile failure, just with an unhelpful error message instead
// of the clear "not enough internal zero-page scratch configured"
// diagnostic the fix direction calls for.
//
// This snippet needs a project file that's missing all 4 zeropage_internal
// keys (2_62_sqrt_missing_zp_scratch.trse, alongside this file) instead of
// the shared project.trse every other snippet uses; run_regressions.sh
// picks it up automatically (a <stem>.trse file next to a snippet
// overrides the shared project.trse).
//
// Method B: compile-error check, no VICE step. Pre-fix: fails with the
// wrong/confusing "sty type 0" opcode error. Post-fix (once the bare
// `return;` becomes a real ErrorHandler::e.Error(...) call): still a
// compile error - this project genuinely lacks the 4 zero-page scratch
// slots Sqrt needs - but with the correct, documented diagnostic instead.
var
	value : integer;
	result : byte;

begin
	value := 200;
	result := Sqrt(value);
	loop();
end.
